<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvaro Arzú</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a>–<a href="/years/2018">2018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvaro Arzú (1946–2018) was a Guatemalan politician who served as president from 1996 to 2000 and for several terms as mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a>. His government concluded the peace negotiations with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> coalition <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemalan-national-revolutionary-unity">URNG</a>, signing the final agreement that ended the 36-year civil war in December 1996. He died in office as mayor of the capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvaro-arzu.jpg" alt="Álvaro Arzú" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foto_oficial_de_Presidente_%C3%81lvaro_Arz%C3%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
